from the time token embedding\n- self-attention over spatial tokens (patchified image tokens)\n- MLP\n\nActually, in DiT, \"time attention\" isn't a standard term. The question says \"replace the time attention mechanism with a non-causal Hyena operator at the place of time attention (setup_4) vs (setup_5)\". Hmm. The researcher's topics are `neurips2024/93022/6:setup_4` and `neurips2024/93022/6:setup_5`. This looks like it references some setup IDs from a NeurIPS 2024 paper (id 93022). I don't know exactly what those setups are. This might be from a hypothetical/paper scenario. I don't have access to that paper. Let me not invent details of setups 4 and 5 — the researcher explicitly says the framework: experiment compares two branches — SiT with original time attention (setup_4) and SiT with non-causal Hyena operator in place of time attention (setup_5).\n\nNote the question budget and actor_step_budget — this is a framework with a question-budget of 6. The researcher's request says: don't give full protocol; do three things; then they will consider before approving the main work on final design. Since `continue_after_initial_plan: false`, after I hand off the plan, the researcher will decide.\n\nActually the parameter `continue_after_initial_plan: false` might mean I shouldn't continue after handing off the initial plan. So I should do the exploration, hand off a plan, and end.\n\nNow, about \"time attention\" in SiT: In the context of trajectory generation, a common transformation of SiT/DiT for sequential data is to treat the sequence of tokens as \"time\" dimension... Hmm. Actually the question is about \"generating extremely long, consistent trajectories that capture dynamics over multiple timescales\". So the model is used to generate trajectories (e.g., time series). In such a setting, \"time attention\" could refer to attention operating across the temporal dimension of the trajectory tokens (as opposed to spatial attention within a frame/state). So the SiT